# Cline Rules

## File Editing

- Always use replace_in_file for targeted edits — never rewrite full files unless explicitly asked.
- If a file exceeds 100 lines, edit only the affected block.

## Task Planning

- For tasks involving 3+ files or unclear requirements, ask all clarifying questions before writing any code.

## Context Management

- If conversation exceeds 50 tool calls, suggest starting a new chat.

## Coding Behavior

- Modify only what is required.
- Reuse existing project patterns and architecture.
- Never expose API keys in frontend code.

## Communication

- Be concise and direct.
- Do not restate the user's request or summarize completed actions.
- If user asks a question without requesting changes, respond with text only — no file changes.
- Ask at most one clarifying question if needed.

## Vue / Ionic / Firebase

- Prefer Composition API patterns already present in the project.
- Prefer incremental UI edits over complete redesigns.

## Email Templates

- Use hex colors only — no rgba() in main backgrounds.
